  "story": {
    "outcome": [
      {
        "text": "70-17-0 in official play; ranked 4 of the pooled top 20 (OPR 335.40, Galileo).",
        "basis": "record",
        "src": [
          "s1",
          "s2"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "bet": [
      {
        "text": "A fixed shooter and a simpler design, after the team debated an ambitious turret.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s13"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "demand": [
      {
        "text": "Fast, consistent autos and accurate shots all match, which made knowing the robot's position at all times one of the most important control goals. The robot also had to fit under the trench, full, with the intake folded.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s13"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "auto": [
      {
        "text": "Each routine is split into parts joined at safe points, and a part starts only when the last one ends, so a crash at midfield does not end it.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s13"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The robot starts under the trench with its intake already pointing to midfield.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s17"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "cycle": [
      {
        "text": "The four-bar intake feeds a roller floor, an entry roller and the drum. The shoot control lines the robot up with the hub, spins up the rollers, moves the hood once they are at speed, then feeds. The driver has three controls: intake up, intake down, shoot.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s13"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "fallback": [
      {
        "text": "In a New England Burns division match its collector was damaged, so it defended while partners scored, and the alliance came back, a commentator says.",
        "basis": "observer",
        "src": [
          "s15"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "It can pass the full field if necessary.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s18"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "changed": [
      {
        "text": "Nightshade had a double shooter and double spindexer; the drum came with the WPI rebuild.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s13"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "At Week 0 Nightshade did not fit under the trench with its intake retracted.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s23"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Ball path, drop-in space and stability problems were a big reason for an 11-day rebuild before WPI, which kept swerves, belly pan and most of the intake design.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s19",
          "s20"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Off-season changes raised about 23 to 26 fuel per second to about 28.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s21",
          "s16"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "functions": [
    {
      "name": "Swerve drive",
      "does": [
        "drive"
      ],
      "type": "swerve",
      "serves": [],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The swerves and belly pan are the only components carried over from Nightshade",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s20"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4-Bar Intake",
      "pieces": [
        "fuel"
      ],
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Let the robot fit under the trench, full, with the intake folded",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "does": [
        "acquire"
      ],
      "type": "four-bar roller intake",
      "serves": [
        "hub"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Two powered rollers driven by two Kraken X60s, with static kicker bars below",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s4",
            "s13"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Roller plates and upper links are SRPP and the bottom link is aluminum, so side hits do not break it",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s4",
            "s13"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A steel-reinforced bash bar protects the front",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "One Kraken X60 deploys it through a MaxSpline shaft under the roller floor and a sprocket bolted to each upper link",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13",
            "s4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Most of the intake was kept the same through the rebuild, with some redesign for the district championship",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s20"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cost": [
        {
          "text": "Finding geometry that cleared the trench in both positions, started inside the frame, folded the kicker bar over the bumpers and kept the links at an angle took a lot of trial and error",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s17"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The motor-to-roller belts had skipping issues and were later switched to #25 chain",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Soon after that switch, made after worlds, a chain slipped off, so flanges were added: 1/8 in polycarbonate discs that sandwich the chain and sprocket",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s22"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The team's theory of the skipping: the motor was pulled toward the roller under torque, which slackened the belt, and a 12 tooth pulley with little wrap made it worse; the roller-to-roller belts did not skip, it assumes because the plate flexed less there",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s22"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Hopper",
      "pieces": [
        "fuel"
      ],
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Carry a full load under the trench",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "does": [
        "retain"
      ],
      "type": "moving and stationary hopper with a stretchy net",
      "serves": [
        "hub"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Roughly 65 fuel in the reveal, roughly 60 in the later slides",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s4",
            "s5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The moving part folds with the intake and stays under trench height deployed and retracted; the stationary part attaches to the bumpers",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s4"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Roller Floor",
      "pieces": [
        "fuel"
      ],
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Move fuel into the shooter with some give, for more throughput",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "does": [
        "transfer"
      ],
      "type": "powered roller floor",
      "serves": [
        "hub"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Two motors drive the floor and loader; three through-shafts carry squish wheels near the entry",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13",
            "s4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Other rollers are 1/32 in wall aluminum with silicone tubing on dead-axle stubs",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Belt distances are shortened to reduce current draw, by",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s4"
          ],
          "value": 0.03,
          "unit": "in"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Entry roller",
      "pieces": [
        "fuel"
      ],
      "does": [
        "transfer"
      ],
      "type": "independently driven roller",
      "serves": [
        "hub"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Driven by its own Kraken X60, separately from the floor, in the reveal before the championship",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s4",
            "s13"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Off-season: spaced 1.5 in compliant wheels, inspired by 2910, replaced the solid roller so balls separate into lanes; accuracy rose significantly at IRI and stayed in the 90% range",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s24",
            "s25"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Off-season: floor and entry roller became one chain-driven system at 1:1, which raised the maximum floor speed; first at about 26 to 28 fuel per second but not very accurate until the shooter was regeared",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s24",
            "s25"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cost": [
        {
          "text": "Off-season: over a long run the combined drive's chain touched itself, from imperfect center distances and a loose chain",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s25"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Full Width Hooded Drum Shooter",
      "pieces": [
        "fuel"
      ],
      "does": [
        "deliver"
      ],
      "type": "full-width drum shooter",
      "serves": [
        "hub"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Four Kraken X60s power the drum, kicker wheel and two hood rollers along a J-shaped path",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13",
            "s4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "1/16 in aluminum tube drum with CatTongue tape, and a custom flywheel",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A printed part added after WPI presses fuel against the back plates to stop it wiggling",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Off-season: a ratio between drum and kicker roller brought their surface speeds closer, added torque and cut the speed variations seen in shot accuracy",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s24",
            "s25"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As of the off-season, the drum starts from zero for every shot: it has too little mass for idling to help, and the kicker drum adds friction",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s26"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Off-season 'flywheel holder': bearings on a sliding mount tension a fast belt, with lock washers against the plate to stop sliding; accuracy improved with less backlash and short testing found no problems",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s27",
            "s28",
            "s24"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cost": [
        {
          "text": "Before that tensioner its belt had too much slack and, at its speed, shredded itself over time",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s27"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Off-season brownouts near the ends of matches, the team thinks, came from the shooter not sustaining its speed, made worse by a slightly decreased hood angle with more power on some shots",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s25"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Hood",
      "pieces": [
        "fuel"
      ],
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Keep the shot angle consistent",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "does": [
        "position"
      ],
      "type": "rack-driven adjustable hood",
      "serves": [
        "hub"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "3D-printed segments between 1/16 in aluminum plates",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The segments were printed roughly on purpose so the gear meshes with less backlash",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The rack is 20 DP",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The racks worked out great: the printed segment is 1/4 in thick, and the plates bolted around it keep its teeth from shearing",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s29"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Localization and shoot sequence",
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Make autos consistent, and shots accurate from anywhere",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "does": [
        "sense"
      ],
      "type": "three-camera pose with staged shot",
      "serves": [
        "hub"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Three cameras keep track of the field position",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Rollers feed only once heading, shooter speed and hood are in tolerance",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s13"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "choice": "Fixed shooter",
      "because": "the team chose a simpler design",
      "instead_of": "an ambitious turret",
      "basis": "team",
      "src": [
        "s13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "Rebuild after week 3",
      "because": "ball path, drop-in space and overall stability problems with the spindexer were a big reason (fuel jammed between its Kraken and the shooter's entry roller; mounted to the belly pan it flexed, which upset tension and made bearings pop out, and the team would now consider a crossmember or frame rail), and the team thought it could do better by starting again somewhat from scratch",
      "basis": "team",
      "src": [
        "s19",
        "s30"
      ],
      "instead_of": "fixing the first robot's problems one by one"
    },
    {
      "choice": "Fixed kicker bars",
      "because": "less compression significantly increased throughput",
      "instead_of": "a powered bottom roller",
      "basis": "team",
      "src": [
        "s13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "SRPP intake roller plates",
      "because": "they are less fragile",
      "instead_of": "polycarbonate",
      "cost": "SRPP deforms permanently, so polycarbonate plates were added where power transmission needs tension (slides that include off-season changes)",
      "basis": "team",
      "src": [
        "s5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "Autos in parts with safe points",
      "because": "a routine can still finish after a collision",
      "instead_of": "one very long path",
      "basis": "team",
      "src": [
        "s13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "Full-width live axles on the intake",
      "because": "cutting a shaft to length was the fastest solution",
      "instead_of": "stub axles",
      "cost": "stubs would have made roller width changes much easier; the team would consider them in the future",
      "basis": "team",
      "src": [
        "s20",
        "s22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "Students set the rebuild schedule, with a date after which the first robot would stay together",
      "because": "it can be easier to hold each other accountable to goals the students set themselves",
      "basis": "team",
      "src": [
        "s32"
      ]
    }
  ],
